{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["ארמי אובד אבי — my father Avraham was an Aramean, אובד — wandering and exiled from the land of Aram. As it is written: לך לך מארצך. And as it is written: ויהי כאשר התעו אותי אלהים מבית אבי — the language of אובד and תועה are one and the same for a person who is exiled, as it is written: תעיתי כשה אובד בקש עבדך. צאן אובדות היו עמי — their shepherds led them astray, that is to say, from a foreign land our fathers came to this land and the Holy One, blessed be He, gave it to us."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:28.913850809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}